[h1]Harmony[/h1]
[b]Europa Universalis IV, made better from within.[/b] Crisp Chinese, Japanese and Korean text, no restarts when returning to the main menu, faster late-game ticks, fewer engine bugs, and richer mods — with game rules untouched.

[b]Important — before starting:[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Subscribing alone does not activate Harmony.[/b] Copy one file ([b]version.dll[/b]) into your EU4 folder once via the one-line PowerShell command or 3-step guide below. Future updates are automatic.
[*][b]Antivirus note:[/b] Harmony is open source (MIT) and loads into [b]eu4.exe[/b] via [b]version.dll[/b], which can occasionally trigger heuristic warnings. Inspect the code on GitHub, add an exclusion for the EU4 folder, or build from source.
[/list]

Your translation mod still supplies translations; mods made for the old double-byte patch — and their saves — work directly.

[h2]What Harmony improves over unmodified EU4[/h2]
[table]
[tr]
[th]Area[/th]
[th]Unmodified EU4[/th]
[th]With Harmony[/th]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]CJK text & fonts[/b][/td]
[td]Broken CJK text without old patches; blurry bitmap fonts, broken line wraps and search.[/td]
[td]Native UTF-8 CJK rendering with system fonts plus free bundled defaults for Simplified Chinese, Japanese and Korean, live font preview, clean wrapping, IME input, and East Asian dates/names.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]Returning & loading[/b][/td]
[td]Returning to the main menu restarts the game; Ironman blocks loading.[/td]
[td]Return to the main menu in seconds without restarting; load saves directly in Ironman (optional auto-save first).[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]Performance[/b][/td]
[td]Late-game stutter, long save freezes, and uncapped menu CPU usage.[/td]
[td]Faster daily/monthly ticks, multi-threaded saving, smarter frame rate cap, and smoother map zoom.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]Bug fixes & QoL[/b][/td]
[td]Duplicate heir names, uneven music loudness, steep volume sliders, reload leaks, Ironman-only achievements.[/td]
[td]Fixes duplicate heir names and reload leaks; equalized music loudness, natural volume sliders, and optional relaxed achievement rules.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td][b]Mods[/b][/td]
[td]Limited to Paradox script files.[/td]
[td]Sandboxed Lua extensions with native-style panels and transparent permission disclosures.[/td]
[/tr]
[/table]

[h2]Installing (pick either option)[/h2]
First, [b]subscribe to Harmony[/b] here and let Steam finish downloading. Then copy [b]version.dll[/b] into your game folder once:

[b]Option A — One-line PowerShell copy (fastest, optional)[/b]
Press [b]Win + X[/b] → [b]Terminal[/b] (or [b]Windows PowerShell[/b]), paste this line and press Enter. It only locates your Steam libraries locally, backs up any existing [b]version.dll[/b] to [b]version.dll.bak[/b], and copies Harmony's [b]version.dll[/b] (nothing is downloaded):
[code]$s=(gp HKCU:\Software\Valve\Steam).SteamPath; $libs=@($s)+((sls '"path"\s+"([^"]+)"' "$s\steamapps\libraryfolders.vdf" -EA 0|%{$_.Matches[0].Groups[1].Value -replace '\\\\','\'})|?{$_}); $g=$libs|%{"$_\steamapps\common\Europa Universalis IV"}|?{Test-Path "$_\eu4.exe"}|select -First 1; $src=$libs|%{"$_\steamapps\workshop\content\236850\3837775887\version.dll"}|?{Test-Path $_}|select -First 1; if(!$g -or !$src){throw "Not found (subscribe in Steam first): game='$g' workshop='$src'"}; $dst="$g\version.dll"; if((Test-Path $dst) -and !(Test-Path "$dst.bak") -and (Get-FileHash $dst).Hash -ne (Get-FileHash $src).Hash){Copy-Item $dst "$dst.bak"}; Copy-Item $src $dst -Force; "Installed to $dst"[/code]

[b]Option B — Manual copy (mouse only, 3 steps)[/b]
[olist]
[*]In Steam, right-click [b]Europa Universalis IV[/b] → [b]Manage → Browse local files[/b] to open the game folder.
[*]Open Paradox Launcher → [b]Mod library[/b] → [b]Harmony[/b] → [b]… → Show in folder[/b] (or open [b]steamapps\workshop\content\236850\3837775887[/b]).
[*]Copy [b]version.dll[/b] next to [b]eu4.exe[/b] (Windows may hide extensions and show [b]version[/b] / [b]eu4[/b]; replace any old [b]version.dll[/b] or back it up first).
[/olist]

Launch EU4 as usual. Harmony does not need to be in a playset; mods built on it are enabled like any normal mod. When active, the main menu shows [b]Harmony v…[/b], [b]Mods[/b] and [b]Settings[/b] at bottom-right.

Steam updates Harmony automatically. When an update includes a newer [b]version.dll[/b], Harmony updates your game folder's copy on startup and restarts automatically (notifying you in-game only if the folder is read-only).

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Steam Windows build of Europa Universalis IV [b]1.37.5[/b].
[*]Single player only (multiplayer support is on the way; the Multiplayer button is disabled while active).
[/list]

[h2]FAQ[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]I subscribed — why is Harmony not showing?[/b] Copy [b]version.dll[/b] next to [b]eu4.exe[/b] (Option A or B) and verify Steam Windows EU4 1.37.5.
[*][b]Migrating from the old double-byte patch or bitmap font mods?[/b] Replace old [b]version.dll[/b] with Harmony's, disable old bitmap font mods (they conflict with system fonts), and keep your translation mod. Existing saves load directly.
[*][b]How do I play multiplayer?[/b] Unsubscribe from Harmony or temporarily move [b]version.dll[/b] out of the game folder.
[*][b]Are saves safe if I disable Harmony later?[/b] Harmony itself does not break saves, though custom text typed with Harmony is stored in UTF-8 (garbled without Harmony). Harmony mods storing their own save data may not load without Harmony.
[*][b]Why is sound quieter, or why did non-Ironman achievements not apply to an old save?[/b] Volume sliders use a smoother quadratic curve, so values under 100 sound quieter until adjusted once. Relaxed achievement rules apply to new campaigns.
[*][b]How do I uninstall cleanly?[/b] Unsubscribe and delete [b]version.dll[/b] from the game folder (restore [b]version.dll.bak[/b] if kept). If you enabled crash dumps in [b]Harmony settings → Advanced[/b], click [b]Disable Windows crash dumps for EU4 (admin)[/b] there first.
[/list]

[h2]Troubleshooting & feedback[/h2]
Open [b]Harmony settings → About[/b] and click [b]Save troubleshooting files to the desktop[/b] for a compact zip (under 24 MB, no saves, username paths redacted, crash dumps slimmed), then attach it on [url=https://github.com/KisinTheFlame/eu4-harmony/issues]GitHub Issues[/url]. You can also open the log folder from [b]Harmony settings → Advanced[/b].

[h2]For mod authors[/h2]
Harmony mods are standard Paradox mods with sandboxed Lua extensions and native-style UI panels. See the [url=https://github.com/KisinTheFlame/eu4-harmony]GitHub README[/url] for documentation and tools.
